24	                                                                                     Abstract
25	
26	                                           We study the large D effective theory for D dimensional charged (Anti) de Sitter black holes.
27	                                           Then we show that the de Sitter Reissner-Nordstrom black hole becomes unstable against
28	                                           gravitational perturbations at larger charge than a critical charge in a higher dimension.
29	                                           Furthermore we find that there is a non-trivial zero-mode static perturbation at the critical
30	                                           charge. The existence of static perturbations suggests the appearance of non-spherical sym-
31	                                           metric solution branches of static charged de Sitter black holes. This expectation is confirmed
32	                                           by constructing the non-spherical symmetric static solutions of large D effective equations.
33	1       Introduction
