19	                                         Abstract: Static, asymptotically flat, non-Schwarzschild black holes in four-dimensional
20	                                         Einstein–Weyl gravity have previously been constructed by numerical shooting, while the
21	                                         local field equations admit horizon and asymptotic expansions to all orders. We give a
22	                                         computer assisted existence proof for a non-Schwarzschild solution whose dimensionless
23	                                         horizon radius is one in units of the massive spin-two scale, with parameters close to the
24	                                         previously reported numerical branch. The exterior is divided into a convergent horizon
25	                                         series domain, a compact core enclosed by a parameter dependent Taylor model with
26	                                         directed rounding, and an infinite asymptotic domain treated as a centered stable manifold
27	                                         fixed point problem. The resulting five-dimensional matching map between the core and tail
28	                                         is continuous on a rigorously specified box. After exact rational preconditioning, the signs
29	                                         on opposite faces satisfy the hypotheses of the Poincaré–Miranda theorem and therefore
30	                                         certify a matching zero. The solution has a regular nondegenerate horizon, no additional
31	                                         exterior horizon, vanishing Ricci scalar, and nonvanishing Ricci tensor. The strict bounds
32	                                         also imply existence at every sufficiently nearby horizon radius and a local continuous family
33	                                         at fixed coupling. The proof establishes existence, but not uniqueness of the matching zero.
34	
35	                                         Keywords: Black Holes, Classical Theories of Gravity
36	Contents
