8	       Abstract. We consider the subextremal Reissner–Nordström–de Sitter black hole whose
9	       horizons are at r− = 19/20, r+ = 1 and rc = 2, with cosmological constant Λ = 1200/4301.
10	       We prove that every nonzero quasinormal mode of the massless scalar wave equation on its
11	       exterior, for every angular momentum ℓ, satisfies Im ω < − 35 κ− , where κ− is the surface
12	       gravity of the Cauchy horizon. The frequency ω = 0 occurs only for ℓ = 0, with a constant
13	       mode, and is a simple zero. By a theorem of Hintz and Vasy, solutions with smooth initial
14	                                                           1
15	       data then extend across the Cauchy horizon in Hloc     and are continuous up to it, so the
16	       Christodoulou formulation of strong cosmic censorship fails for this linear model at this
17	       parameter point. Bounded frequencies and low angular momenta are handled by interval-
18	       arithmetic certificates for the radial Wronskian. All remaining frequencies are excluded
19	       by a Hermite-type monotone quantity integrated along complex contours in the tortoise
20	       coordinate. This quantity gives certificates that hold uniformly in ℓ ≥ 10, so the infinitely
21	       many angular momenta are covered by finitely many interval computations. The certificates
22	       and the programs that check them are in the supplement.
