8	       Abstract. We prove that the singly spinning Myers–Perry black hole in seven spacetime
9	       dimensions with rotation parameter a/r+ = 8 is linearly unstable in the sense of Prabhu and
10	       Wald. We construct smooth, compactly supported, constraint-satisfying initial data that are
11	       invariant under U (1) × SO(4) and odd under the (t-ϕ) reflection. For their gauge-fixed repre-
12	       sentative P ′ we establish that the potential energy of KP ′ , the initial time derivative of the
13	       corresponding solution, is negative. Positivity of the kinetic energy makes the Rayleigh–Ritz
14	       quotient ω 2 of Prabhu and Wald negative, and their variational principle gives exponential
15	       growth of the kinetic energy of the time derivative of the solution. We identify this potential
16	       energy with the local canonical energy of the evolved compactly supported data, by an ar-
17	       gument that uses only identities from the Prabhu–Wald framework. The trial is explicit; the
18	       negativity is established by a computer-assisted certificate: a rigorous adaptive quadrature in
19	       which the integrand is bounded on complex polydiscs by bivariate Taylor models with inter-
20	       val remainders. The certified value is a small residue of large contributions of both signs, and
21	       its sign relies on the exactness of the symbolic derivation; we state this dependence explicitly.
22	       The certificate, its records and the programs that check them are in the supplement.
