9	                                        Abstract: About twenty years ago, Choptuik studied numerically the gravi-
10	                                        tational collapse (Einstein field equations) of a massless scalar field in spheri-
11	                                        cal symmetry, and found strong evidence for a universal, self-similar solution
12	                                        at the threshold of black hole formation. We prove rigorously the existence of
13	                                        a real analytic solution, that we interpret as the solution observed by Chop-
14	                                        tuik. Our construction covers an open neighborhood of the past light cone of
15	                                        the singularity. The proof is computer assisted. Starting from an explicit ap-
16	                                        proximate solution, we show that nearby there is a true solution. The source
17	                                        code and a high precision data file (about 80 significant decimal digits, with
18	                                        rigorous error bounds) are included. We do not study perturbations.
