13	                                                                                                  Abstract
14	                                                    We give a rigorous, constructive proof that there exists a Ricci-flat Kähler metric on the
15	                                                Fermat quartic hypersurface, independently of Yau’s famous theorem, along with an explicit
16	                                                and accurate analytic approximation to the metric. The proof combines numerical techniques to
17	                                                obtain the approximately Ricci flat metric, a fixed point theorem to prove existence, and verified
18	                                                numerics to get the bounds used by the fixed point theorem. The method is general and we
19	                                                discuss the computational issues in applying it to other manifolds.
