8	                                                Abstract. We present a new framework for characterizing quasinormal modes (QNMs) or resonant
9	                                                states for the wave equation on asymptotically flat spacetimes, applied to the setting of extremal
10	                                                Reissner–Nordström black holes. We show that QNMs can be interpreted as honest eigenfunctions
11	                                                of generators of time translations acting on Hilbert spaces of initial data, corresponding to a suitable
12	                                                time slicing. The main difficulty that is present in the asymptotically flat setting, but is absent in the
13	                                                previously studied asymptotically de Sitter or anti de Sitter sub-extremal black hole spacetimes, is that
14	                                                L2 -based Sobolev spaces are not suitable Hilbert space choices. Instead, we consider Hilbert spaces
15	                                                of functions that are additionally Gevrey regular at infinity and at the event horizon. We introduce
16	                                                L2 -based Gevrey estimates for the wave equation that are intimately connected to the existence of
17	                                                conserved quantities along null infinity and the event horizon. We relate this new framework to the
