14	                                                                                   Abstract
15	                                                We prove that there are no exponentially growing modes nor modes on the real
16	                                             axis for the Teukolsky equation on Kerr black hole spacetimes, both in the extremal
17	                                             and subextremal case. We also give a quantitative refinement of mode stability. As an
18	                                             immediate application, we show that the transmission and reflection coefficients of the
19	                                             scattering problem are bounded, independently of the specific angular momentum of
20	                                             the black hole, in any compact set of real frequencies excluding zero frequency and the
21	                                             superradiant threshold.
22	                                                While in the subextremal setting these results were known previously, the extremal
23	                                             case is more involved and has remained an open problem. Ours are the first results
24	                                             outside axisymmetry and could serve as a preliminary step towards understanding
25	                                             boundedness, scattering and decay properties of general solutions to the Teukolsky
26	                                             equation on extremal Kerr black holes.
