16	                                                                                           Abstract
17	
18	                                            In this work, we investigate the correspondence between quasinormal modes (QNMs) and greybody factors
19	                                         (GBFs) in higher-dimensional Reissner–Nordstöm–de Sitter black holes based on the massless scalar field. Our
20	                                         analysis focuses on the QNMs in the near-ultracold family where the inner, outer, and cosmological horizons
21	                                         are close together. Under the geometric limit condition, the leading-order Wentzel–Kramers–Brillouin term of
22	                                         the QNM is dominant for fixed angular quantum numbers and dimensionality without imposing the eikonal
23	                                         limit. Particularly, the corresponding GBFs also retain the explicit form of both parameters. Furthermore, we
24	                                         demonstrate that the half-transmission frequency of the GBF and its derivative are related to null geodesics, in
25	                                         terms of aspects such as the angular frequency and Lyapunov exponent, with the use of both parameters. We
26	                                         provide their relationships in arbitrary dimensionality. Furthermore, the higher-order corrections to the QNMs
27	                                         are investigated at the Nariai limit and in the near-ultracold geometry with separated horizons.
